error[E0277]: `i64` cannot be recorded as a histogram value
 --> tests/compile_fail/signed_where_unsigned.rs:5:5
  |
5 |     switchgear_metrics::histogram!("m", -3i64);
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ histograms take an unsigned integer, a float, or a Duration
  |
  = help: the trait `switchgear_metrics::value::HistogramValue` is not implemented for `i64`
  = note: tracing-opentelemetry has no i64 histogram: a signed value is silently recorded as an attribute, not a metric
  = note: cast explicitly if you meant it, e.g. `value as u64` or `value as f64`
  = help: the following other types implement trait `switchgear_metrics::value::HistogramValue`:
            f32
            f64
            u16
            u32
            u64
            u8
            usize
  = note: this error originates in the macro `$crate::histogram` which comes from the expansion of the macro `switchgear_metrics::histogram` (in Nightly builds, run with -Z macro-backtrace for more info)

